=== Negative items ===
* {{dlc|anr}} The {{i|D4}} and the {{i|D100}} will reroll the Holy Mantle The Lost starts with after giving the Greed Machine 879 coins.
** {{Dlc|r}}If {{Achievement|Lost holds Holy Mantle}} is unlocked, the starting Holy Mantle cannot be rerolled anymore.
* {{i|Ankh}}, {{t|Broken Ankh}}, {{i|Judas' Shadow}} and {{i|Lazarus' Rags}} grant extra lives but respawn The Lost as {{C|???}}, {{C|Black Judas}}, or {{C|Lazarus Risen}} respectively, which will cause the game to treat them as these characters instead of The Lost. It is suggested to avoid these three items altogether if the player is interested in gaining The Lost exclusive achievements and/or completion marks.
* {{i|Dark Bum}} no longer maintains its main benefit of providing {{e|Soul Heart}}s as they are now useless. While it may spawn a friendly spider, it is also likely to spawn an enemy spider, which can instantly kill The Lost if the player is not careful.
** {{Dlc|r}} Dark Bum now has a 20% chance to spawn a random pill, card or rune, making it slightly more useful for The Lost.
** With {{i|Immaculate Conception}}, Dark Bum will be useful to convert useless Red Hearts to useful Soul Hearts. However, the player must still be careful of {{E|Spider}}s.
* {{i|Isaac's Heart}}, while having many useful synergies {{dlc|na}} as well as the added benefit of immunity to Brimstone lasers, makes dodging more difficult in many scenarios, leading many players to take damage when they otherwise would not have. It is also very difficult to avoid a stray laser from an {{E|Eye}}, as The Lost cannot block this shot and protect Isaac's Heart from it. Also, there is a chance it can spawn atop an Eye in the It Lives! fight, leading to a very cheap and unavoidable death.
* Any explosive items, such as {{i|Anarchist Cookbook}}, {{i|Curse of the Tower}}, or {{i|Ipecac}} should be used with extreme care.
** If the player chooses to pick up {{i|Ipecac}}, they should not pick up {{i|Loki's Horns}} or {{i|Mom's Eye}}, as an unexpected shot against a wall will lead to instant death. {{i|Lost Contact}} is also problematic as it can cause explosions to happen in closer proximity to the player than desired.
* Items that work by causing self-damage, such as the {{i|IV Bag}}, {{i|Blood Rights}} or {{i|Razor Blade}} will end the run if used and must be avoided. {{i|Dead Sea Scrolls}} also has the potential to prematurely end a run if {{i|Kamikaze!}} is triggered and the player doesn't have its Holy Mantle active. {{Dlc|nr}}{{i|Isaac's Heart}} will allow The Lost to use these items without taking damage.
* {{i|Bucket of Lard}} reduces speed by 0.2 and does not provide any benefit.
* {{i|Glyph of Balance|dlc=nr}} will replace all room clear and champion drops with soul hearts, resulting in much less pickups throughout the run.
* {{i|Leo}} and {{i|Thunder Thighs}} are not great as they remove The Lost's ability to use [[obstacle]]s to his advantage, as they can break these obstacles. Also, stepping on a [[Rocks#Mushrooms|poisonous mushroom]], or carelessly stepping on a [[Bomb Rock]] can end a run. The only benefit is the small chance of finding a trapdoor or items like {{i|Dry Baby}} or {{i|The Small Rock}} when breaking said obstacles.
* {{i|Strange Attractor}}: Unpredictably pulls enemies towards The Lost, especially floating enemies like {{E|Boom Fly|text=Boom Flies}}. It's advised to avoid this item unless The Lost has {{i|The Ludovico Technique}}, as both items combined may create a powerful synergy.
** {{Dlc|r}} Strange Attractor now pulls enemies towards where the magnetic tear lands, making it safer to take.
* {{I|Proptosis}} may seem useful because it doubles your damage, but it requires you to get closer to enemies, resulting in you being more likely to get hit.
** {{I|Lost Contact}} / [[Familiar|Orbitals]] nullify this a bit, but you still have to get close to enemies.
* {{i|Ocular Rift}}, as it can uncontrollably pull enemies around, especially with items like {{I|Loki's Horns}} or {{I|Mom's Eye}}, though it can also be very useful in avoiding damage when played right.

